# Access control

Full spec: **[docs/access-control.md](../docs/access-control.md)** · Prescriptive gaps: **[docs/gaps/actions-audit.md](../docs/gaps/actions-audit.md)**

## One action ID

- Same **`ActionName`** from `packages/actions` for RBAC, UI `useCan`, audit, MCP, and oRPC.
- No separate ABAC-only IDs.

## Server

- Mutations: **`runAction`** in `module/shared/server/run-action.ts` (permission + audit + ServiceResponse).
- Expected deny → **`ServiceResponse` `failed`**, not throw to client.
- **`buildAccessContext`** supplies org/project/team/user fields per action scope.

## Client

- Gate with **`useCan` / `<Can>`** only — server still enforces.
- Do not branch on raw role strings in feature UI.

